	"note": "Timed effects (D-052, compounding D-082). Started by items whose use block has \"effect\": id (+ optional \"doses\", default 1). seconds = time per dose; doses add up to max_doses; strength = 1 + gain x (doses - 1), and fades out as the last dose wears off. hold_from / hold_seconds: at that many doses the level holds before wearing off. mods multiply at strength 1 and scale with strength: damage_taken, move_speed, hunger_drain, thirst_drain; heal_per_second adds HP; fov_add widens the view; tint [r,g,b,a] colours the screen (alpha scales with strength), pulse_hz > 0 cycles the hue. look (per strength, or [per, from] = only above `from`): sway_deg camera roll, drift_deg_s the view wanders (aim too), stumble pushes your walking sideways (0-1), double_px double vision, blur blurred edges (0-1), lurch sudden view jolts (0-1), impair disc throw error + power bar jitter (0-1). vomit {from (strength), every_s [min, max], food, water, stop_s}. When an effect runs out, its \"after\" effect starts at after_scale x the peak doses. Not saved.",
